course: dictionary
lesson: 12836
title: Words that wrap things up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in one go. «Encased» is one of them. Break it into parts: en- means put into, and case means a box or cover. So encased means put inside a case, or completely covered by something hard.
explain: «The fly was encased in amber for millions of years.» Amber is a hard, clear, golden stone, so the fly was sealed inside it. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "The fly was completely covered by something hard for millions of years." It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: «Her broken arm was encased in plaster while it healed.» The plaster is hard and covers the arm all the way round, so it protects the arm. Encase is the base word, and encased is its past form.
fact: Encase means to cover or surround something completely with something hard or protective.
fact: «Encased» means completely covered or surrounded by something hard, or put inside a case or shell.
fact: «Encased in ice» means frozen inside ice, and «encased in amber» means sealed inside hard, clear tree resin.
fact: «Encased in armour» means wearing a hard metal covering for protection.
fact: Look for clues: hard things around something, like ice, stone, metal or plaster, show that encased means covered and protected.
exercise: «The ancient bug was encased in amber.» What does encased mean here? | Cooked slowly | *Completely covered by something hard | Painted bright red | Carried off by a bird
exercise: «The knight was encased in armour from head to toe.» What is the armour doing? | Keeping him hidden in a tent | Making him lighter so he can run faster | *Protecting him with a hard metal covering | Showing his favourite colour
exercise: Find and copy the word that means completely covered: «The tiny frog was encased in a shell of ice.» | tiny | ice | *encased | frog
test: «The chocolate egg was encased in shiny foil.» What does encased mean? | *Completely covered | Opened carefully | Eaten quickly | Put on a shelf
test: Ella says, «My broken leg is encased in plaster.» What does that tell you? | The leg is lost | The leg can run faster | *The leg is covered and protected by hard plaster | The leg is painted
exam: «Scientists found a bee encased in amber, perfectly preserved.» What does encased mean? | Flying high above the trees | Dancing with the other bees | Lost in a forest | *Completely covered and sealed inside something hard
